# CelesTrak GP data, FORMAT=CSV: one data row (one element set). Public. Maintained by hand.
# The columns are in the order of the header row CelesTrak sends (pack.md, Column order);
# the header row is not a message of this pack.
format        celestrak-gp-csv
version       0.1.0
distribution  public
source        "CelesTrak, A New Way to Obtain GP Data (https://celestrak.org/NORAD/documentation/gp-data-formats.php, updated 2026-06-23, read 2026-11-21): the CSV form uses the OMM keywords; column order and number notation as the CSV response of 2026-11-21 shows them"
source        "CCSDS 502.0-B-3 Orbit Data Messages, April 2023 (https://ccsds.org/Pubs/502x0b3e1.pdf), tables 4-2 and 4-3: the meaning and unit of each keyword"
uses          ckgp
uses          ckgpcsv
wire          text

field  ckgp.object_name              0   string
field  uid                           1   string
field  ckgp.object_id                1   string
field  ckgp.epoch                    2   string
field  ckgp.mean_motion              3   float
field  ckgp.eccentricity             4   float
field  ckgp.inclination              5   float
field  ckgp.ra_of_asc_node           6   float
field  ckgp.arg_of_pericenter        7   float
field  ckgp.mean_anomaly             8   float
field  ckgp.ephemeris_type           9   int
field  ckgp.classification_type      10  string
field  ckgp.norad_cat_id             11  int
field  ckgp.element_set_no           12  int
field  ckgp.rev_at_epoch             13  int
field  ckgpcsv.bstar_text            14  string
field  ckgpcsv.mean_motion_dot_text  15  string
field  ckgpcsv.mean_motion_ddot_text 16  string
